#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:5
#: 661cbf6f8fd64a4cb62a9fc5f610cb90
msgid "Proximity Sensors (landing page)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:7
#: 74b10ce48d8f47f0a4c9f60cb0fdd549
msgid "Copter/Rover have support for avoidance obstacles that may appear in front of the vehicle. The first step to enable these features is to have a working Proximity Sensor. ArduPilot supports up to 4 sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:9
#: 282e9d8972614f5295e48fb20b210731
msgid "360 degree Lidars are typically used in object avoidance as proximity sensors, but multiple rangefinders sensors or stereo depth cameras can also be used for proximity detection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:13
#: 274c3af105fe45fc8d92dc3aad0c1001
msgid "Users often confuse RangeFinders with proximity sensors. Rangefinders are typically single dimensional sensors, that provide distances from a very narrow ray. Proximity Sensors is generally a name used for 360 Lidar and other sensors with a wider FOV. The settings and parameters used for both classes of sensors are different."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:16
#: a3fc31961cca4f02bc679d2f592ed027
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:18
#: 98fb3af04a19449694ec0d4b46027ec4
msgid "You will need to set up the parameter ``PRXx_TYPE`` correctly for the sensor(s) you are using. Exclusion zones are provided for 360 degree Lidars, since these may have obstructions in their field of view. Exclusion zones are set via the ``PRXx_IGN_ANGx`` and ``PRXx_IGN_WIDx`` parameters, specifying a direction and width the frame obstruction presents and will be ignored. Up to 6 exclusion sectors can be specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:21
#: 14ba9f72650540b2957aac9e798f8949
msgid "A list of supported units is shown on the :ref:`common-rangefinder-landingpage` under \"Omnidirectional Proximity Rangefinders\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:24
#: c306f6c1e0a849f0a59fc91035b092f9
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:27
#: efbeeeec6fbf44f8982b25169c13f1d6
msgid "Real-time view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:29
#: 969fc6c179874008a352802d90fb6b22
msgid "Real-time distances can be seen in the Mission Planner's proximity viewer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:37
#: 2287f2b39c0746af911515d20c7469ec
msgid "Press the plus and minus key while the proximity window is open to change the range of the display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:41
#: 7e99097e8cb14d8d84bb8e4dc988a3ae
msgid "This window can be opened by moving to the MP's Flight Data screen, press Ctrl-F and push the Proximity button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:48
#: 15fc255f6a86403a8b5bc7a5b0f3ae15
msgid "DataFlash logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:50
#: e7ccc9339248455587daae88a72da9e6
msgid "Upward and downward facing range finder distances can be seen in the DataFlash Log's RFND message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:52
#: 7257a5042c854e97a032b42fb3244317
msgid "The distance to the nearest object in 8 quadrants around the vehicle is recorded in the DataFlash log's PRX messages. Since Copter and Rover have the ability to store 3D obstacles, various instances of PRX message log is used. 0th instance stands for obstacles detected between -75 to -45 degrees pitch. Similarly, PRX[1] stores from -45 to -15 degrees, and PRX[2] stores from -15 to + 15 degrees and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:56
#: 4584707f8dcf4315b913a6f797900179
msgid "Additional Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:59
#: f22052656f5b41b5b9eef57bfe7f86b5
msgid "Filter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:61
#: dd47278e2b8d4b47b854cdfb446955e2
msgid "Various sensors can be attached to the autopilot. However, depending on the quality and use case of the sensor, it might give noisy data. This noise will be stored onboard the autopilot as \"obstacles\" and the vehicle might suddenly start avoiding false objects. To counter this problem, Copter and Rover have an inbuilt low pass filter on the raw sensor data. The filter can be adjusted by :ref:`PRX_FILT <PRX_FILT>` (setting it to 0 will disable the feature). By default, only the filtered values get logged. However, by setting :ref:`PRX_LOG_RAW <PRX_LOG_RAW>` = 1, raw values from the sensors will also be logged. This can be used for debugging purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:67
#: 4605b7e1e8bb443db546a28ecd216308
msgid "Ground detection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:71
#: 2a3939d69ec74f52990dd508a54d9651
msgid "This feature requires a valid downward facing rangefinder configured first and only works with Copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:73
#: e3782d4e212c4d9a8ba89b9c18fd1a68
msgid "For low altitude obstacle avoidance, and while just taking off and landing, sometimes the sensor will pick up the ground below as obstacle. This can be dangerous because the vehicle will try and \"avoid\" these obstacles (if avoidance features are turned on). By setting :ref:`PRX_IGN_GND <PRX_IGN_GND>` = 1, we attempt to detect and ignore any obstacles that are near the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-proximity-landingpage.rst:78
#: 471ff3d529ed4885ae5c923e4ce99f08
msgid "This feature only works when the vehicle is armed It might also ignore valid obstacles when the vehicle is flying very close to the ground. Detected obstacles will not be visible on the Mission Planner Proximity Viewer, or data flash logs."
msgstr ""
